You complete as many rounds as you can in 20 minutes of 5 parallette handstand push-ups, 10 toes-to-rings and 15 medicine-ball cleans (20 lb / 14 lb). You need a pair of parallettes, a set of rings and a medicine ball. Pressing from parallettes lets your head drop below your hands, so each push-up is longer than one on the floor. The toes-to-rings then work your grip and core.',
   '[{"name": "Parallette Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "5", "tip": "Kick up with your hands on the parallettes and lower your head below your hands, then press to lockout."}, {"name": "Toes-to-Rings", "reps": "10", "tip": "Hang from the rings and lift your toes to touch them. Keep a steady swing."}, {"name": "Medicine Ball Cleans", "reps": "15", "tip": "Squat with the ball between your feet, then stand and pop it to your chest, landing in a squat.", "rx_men": "20 lb", "rx_women": "14 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps.',
