   'time',
   'Lee honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Dick Alson Lee Jr., 31, of Orange Park, Florida, assigned to the 95th Military Police Battalion, 18th Military Police Brigade, 21st Theater Sustainment Command, in Sembach, Germany. He died on April 26, 2012, from injuries sustained when his vehicle encountered an improvised explosive device in Ghazni Province, Afghanistan.

You complete 5 rounds of a 400 m run, 1 deadlift (345 lb / 225 lb), 3 squat cleans and 5 push jerks (185 lb / 125 lb), 3 muscle-ups and 1 rope climb to 15 ft. The reps are low, but the loads are heavy and the gymnastics take skill. Each round mixes running, heavy lifting and gymnastics.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Hold a pace you can repeat. You need to be steady for the lifts after it."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "1", "tip": "One heavy rep. Set your back flat and push the floor away.", "rx_men": "345 lb", "rx_women": "225 lb"}, {"name": "Squat Cleans", "reps": "3", "tip": "Catch the bar in a full front squat. Take them as singles.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Push Jerks", "reps": "5", "tip": "Dip and drive, then punch under the bar and lock out overhead.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Muscle-Ups", "reps": "3", "tip": "Strong kip, pull the rings to your chest and turn over fast."}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "1 to 15 ft", "tip": "Lock the rope with your feet and stand up. Climb down under control."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Do not rush the heavy deadlift", "Take the squat cleans as singles", "Climb down the rope under control"]'::jsonb,
   '["Use two barbells if you have them, one for the deadlift and one for the cleans and jerks.", "Breathe before the deadlift and set your back flat; one good rep beats a rushed one.", "After the third squat clean, you can push jerk the bar straight from the rack position.", "On the muscle-ups, keep the rings close and get your chest over them quickly.", "Shake out your arms on the run so your grip is ready for the rope."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 225 lb / 155 lb and the cleans and jerks to 135 lb / 95 lb, or less. Replace muscle-ups with pull-ups and dips or ring rows. Do a rope climb to a lower height or 3 lying-to-standing rope pulls.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Lee workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of a 400 m run, 1 deadlift (345 lb / 225 lb), 3 squat cleans (185 lb / 125 lb), 5 push jerks (185 lb / 125 lb), 3 muscle-ups and 1 rope climb to 15 ft."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Lee?", "answer": "65 reps: 5 deadlifts, 15 squat cleans, 25 push jerks, 15 muscle-ups and 5 rope climbs, plus 2,000 m of running."}, {"question": "Do I need two barbells?", "answer": "It helps. The deadlift is heavier than the cleans and jerks, so a second bar saves you from changing plates every round."}, {"question": "Who was Lee?", "answer": "U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Dick Alson Lee Jr., 31, of Orange Park, Florida. He died on April 26, 2012, from injuries sustained when his vehicle encountered an improvised explosive device in Ghazni Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
